{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332064-how-magic-impacts-mage-society","id":1332064,"title":"how magic impacts mage society","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-08-21T21:27:29-07:00","id":1332064,"title":"how magic impacts mage society","content":"How do you portray a society made of people that can be unreasonably lucky in social circumstances, or rewind and undo a gaffe, or can speak with TRUTH in their word, or can be so insidiously convincing as to make you kill your own mother? And that's at the low end, what about mages that just warp the social fabric around them to gain prestige and regard as needed (aka Status, Allies, Retainer, and Contact dots).<br /> <br /> Basically, what are the practical implications for a consillium when almost every mage can wield magic to their own social advantage within the consillium?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T21:50:30-07:00","id":1332067,"title":"","content":"Rule no. 1 is Don\u2019t Get Caught. Which if you\u2019re going to be a dick can be pretty difficult since Mages are investigators by nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T22:48:57-07:00","id":1332074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332064-how-magic-impacts-mage-society?p=1332067#post1332067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rule no. 1 is Don\u2019t Get Caught. Which if you\u2019re going to be a dick can be pretty difficult since Mages are investigators by nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what constitutes an offense you can get caught at as opposed to &quot;well that's just expected&quot;? Is it a level of arcana dot used, whether the effect targets yourself as opposed to others? Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T22:50:25-07:00","id":1332075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332064-how-magic-impacts-mage-society?p=1332067#post1332067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rule no. 1 is Don\u2019t Get Caught. Which if you\u2019re going to be a dick can be pretty difficult since Mages are investigators by nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that that's Rule 2, or at least Rule 1.1.<br /> <br /> Rule 1 is, of course, Cornelius's Lament: &quot;The trouble is, the other side can do magic too, Prime Minister.&quot;<br /> <br /> Both revolve around the same thing-anything you can do to be an asshole, others can do too-and given the power of arcane secrets that everyone gathers as well as the semi-inherent hierarchies of mastering the Arcana, there's a fair amount of &quot;Anything you can do, I can do better&quot; with a healthy heaping of &quot;Do you really wanna know what I can do?&quot; style paranoia baked in.<br /> <br /> THis isn't to say that this armed society is always a polite society, or even hyper attentive, but if you're going to be a dumbass and think you can just cheat the game, there's a lot of hands on deck to slap you down. Trying to cheat your way through the ranks and into prestige is a trick and a half, and honestly, you're going to do better by just going at it. Using magic to get in the social edge over others is often a matter of more private, controlled affairs and fair manipulation of the circumstances going on. If you walk into a Caucus meeting with Fate swinging your first impression to perfect for everyone, someone's going to eventually turn your fate into a bunch of tripping wire-but if you use that same fate spell with an influential figure on a damn rough day where his usual circle isn't there, he might not bother with double guessing your perfect opening line.<br /> <br /> Honestly, it gets to a point where trying to use magic to up your game is less effort than just personally upping your game.<br /> <br /> The final notes on the subject is that you actually have a decent contrast between societies on the subject, because the Seers basically do operate by the logic mentioned in the OP, where as the Pentacle tends to take a more rational and less &quot;rarwr&quot; approach to handling things. If people can reasonably assume that the people around them aren't going to bend everything to come out on top, then they reasonably won't act in that way. If people can reasonably assume that the gods of this world only reward first place and any resource not used against others is a resource used against you, then you get a pyramid made of magically enforced Mexican standoffs.<br /> <br /> It's rather like life, that way. Community-minded people build communities, individual-first people build &quot;Fuck you, I got mine&quot; systems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lareath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332064-how-magic-impacts-mage-society?p=1332074#post1332074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But what constitutes an offense you can get caught at as opposed to &quot;well that's just expected&quot;? Is it a level of arcana dot used, whether the effect targets yourself as opposed to others? Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Within the Pentacle, there's the order of Laws described in the Lex Magica that more or less describes the priority of sacred rights and such, as described in the Awakening 2nd Core. I think Sigil and Sanctum goes into it more? I'll admit, I'm not hyper clear on what are specific offenses and such, and my resources are in a box. But that said, those are at least two sources we can point you at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-22-2019, 01:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T23:03:24-07:00","id":1332076,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d say what constitutes an offense is going to come down to whatever the local Lex says because they\u2019ve already had some dealings with dicks, and a matter of personal preference which depending how things go may also become part of the Lex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T23:13:31-07:00","id":1332078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332064-how-magic-impacts-mage-society?p=1332076#post1332076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d say what constitutes an offense is going to come down to whatever the local Lex says because they\u2019ve already had some dealings with dicks, and a matter of personal preference which depending how things go may also become part of the Lex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, 90% of the intrigue is gonna come down to the local Iron and Bronze Laws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T02:25:08-07:00","id":1332094,"title":"","content":"Also it s difficult to totally conceal the use of magic, when in doubt about the nature of a spell one could dispel or counterspell it easily, a council could require the dispelling of suspect spell before entering a sanctum","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T07:11:33-07:00","id":1332122,"title":"","content":"Some wise posts here, I just wanted to post a few things that came up in my own games. <br /> <br /> In my London game I had a large and established consilium that had a number of powerful foes. As a result we had a hard rule against spellcasting or most any magic beyond Mage Sight at consillium meetings and mixers. This included buff spells, so no using mind to max your social stats before your chat with the Herald and so on. I was a little worried that would feel dull, but found my players enjoyed the change of pace and having to occasionally find more grounded means of solving problems. The investigative powers of the average Mage and that no one wanted to piss of the scary chief Sentinel meant that this rule pretty much enforces itself.<br /> <br /> On people using time travel for a do-over, its worth remembering that time travellers are called out as pretty noticable, with everything they change/interact with triggering time sight. I generally play this up at my table, with travelors basically being lit up like lighthouses under AMS. While that does not (and should not) utterly undermine the usefulness of the spell, it does mean a savvy NPC will be able to guess what their dealing with and respond appropriately.<br /> <br /> Magic does and should have an impact on mage society, being able to seal a pact with a binding Oath can help engender trust and keep the peace between diverse groups. Words of Truth and other Prime spells mean that often the best way to manipulate is through cryptic metaphor, dropped hints and tidbits of truth rather than outright lies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T07:16:55-07:00","id":1332123,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna go on a limb and answer the OP's querry with &quot;heavily &quot;. Aside from the thought exercise of how say, 100 mages influence a geographical area, I wouldn't consider it unless it serves the narrative I want to portray.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T09:30:09-07:00","id":1332138,"title":"","content":"<br /> There are a couple dividing lines to consider. The first is what they use their magic to accomplish. If that's good and acceptable it's arguably good and acceptable use of magic. The second is who is being targeted by the magic. First impressions can be achieved by adjusting the mind of the other party, by granting insights into behavior to the person wanting the good impression, by testing multiple approaches and going with the best, or any of a number of other ways. If the magic affects others, it's far more suspect.<br /> <br /> Using magic to improve one's own performance socially is going to tend to be avoiding being abrasive. It's <i>not</i> going to rub people the wrong way <i>by design</i>. Fundamentally, someone else being charming is pleasant. Them avoiding your hot buttons, even if they rely on magic as a crutch to do it, really doesn't seem like something to discourage.<br /> <br /> An upshot would be that such organizations would tend to interact more smoothly than normal. The thoughtful and wise magi would seem remarkably composed and thoughtful because they would be using judicious magic to aid them in just that. Really helpful in keeping a bunch of zealots from competing religions working together, one might imagine.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-25T22:50:00-07:00","id":1332607,"title":"","content":"It's probably important to note survivor bias.<br /> <br /> Every Mage society worth portraying has survived to the present day of your Chronicle (for Time-Arcanum-given values of &quot;present day&quot;). That doesn't mean that most Mage societies have survived: it means that most of them didn't work out and imploded in one manner or another. The structure of the Big Three sects exists because it works. The Lex Magica and the Iron Pyramid are a big deal for precisely that reason.<br /> <br /> The other trick is that Mages are relatively rare. Forumites like to debate the exact numbers and ranges, but it never gets above &quot;small town&quot; numbers. So while there are some trappings of law and higher order societal structure, in most Consilia-sized societies everyone basically knows who you are, who your mentors were, who last owned the Hallows you sup at, etc. There are exceptions, yes, and those people are suspicious precisely because they're an exception.<br /> <br /> If there's any kind of agreement that you're abusing your powers, they can and will track you down and end you. Indeed, most APs I've read have this kind of thing as at least a subplot. (And it usually seems to end with the PCs advocating for some kind of mercy, though sometimes not.)<br /> <br /> What counts as abuse is different in different places, though. You'd expect traveling Mages to make a point of introducing themselves to the Consilia they visit, stating their business, learning the local customs, and to the degree they fail to do this, be regarded with suspicion to hostility.<br /> <br /> So, honestly, the answer is, &quot;Pick up Sigil and Sanctum.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T04:05:43-07:00","id":1332631,"title":"","content":"Magic that influences other Mages directly or indirectly is probably never regarded too favorable.<br /> <br /> I'd say Magic that targets others is always bad, in the sens of ranging from a serious social faux pas to an outright crime.<br /> If you use magic to improve your own performance, I think it depends on how subtle you are about it. Just a little bit here or there, not to much and not to noticeable, your fine. Otherwise you might either become the laughingstock of polite society as the clown coming to every social event heavily enchanted at best or you'd be an ostracized pariah at worst.<br /> Because keep in mind, other Mages know what Mages can do, and so if things seem a little bit to perfect, the might become mistrustful.<br /> <br /> The above describes a working mage community.<br /> <br /> On the other end, you would have a society of paranoia and heavy mistrust, where every interaction with other mages would require heavy regulation.<br /> <br /> There are of course variations and shades between those two but that should give you an idea.<br /> <br /> One analogy you can use is the business world. When people play fair, trust each other don't and try to use every weapon in their arsenal against on another, a handshake is enough. Again on the other end of the spectrum, corporate lawyers go over every minute detail and word of any given contract.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","name":"nobby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T05:10:45-07:00","id":1332637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nobby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332064-how-magic-impacts-mage-society?p=1332631#post1332631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magic that influences other Mages directly or indirectly is probably never regarded too favorable.<br /> <br /> I'd say Magic that targets others is always bad, in the sens of ranging from a serious social faux pas to an outright crime.<br /> If you use magic to improve your own performance, I think it depends on how subtle you are about it. Just a little bit here or there, not to much and not to noticeable, your fine. Otherwise you might either become the laughingstock of polite society as the clown coming to every social event heavily enchanted at best or you'd be an ostracized pariah at worst.<br /> Because keep in mind, other Mages know what Mages can do, and so if things seem a little bit to perfect, the might become mistrustful.<br /> <br /> The above describes a working mage community.<br /> <br /> On the other end, you would have a society of paranoia and heavy mistrust, where every interaction with other mages would require heavy regulation.<br /> <br /> There are of course variations and shades between those two but that should give you an idea.<br /> <br /> One analogy you can use is the business world. When people play fair, trust each other don't and try to use every weapon in their arsenal against on another, a handshake is enough. Again on the other end of the spectrum, corporate lawyers go over every minute detail and word of any given contract.</div> </div> </div> </div>Targeting others is not a problem, depending on the method. Lets say you have an enemy who has sworn yoir death. If your cabal follows the Right of Nemesis, it means he can openly challenge you to a Duel Arcane. Can it be to the death ? Depends on the Consilium, but I would normally say not without a Hierarch's consent and some kind of mediation attempt by the Lex Magicka. The advantage of this custom is that it says to your enemies &quot;form a line and I will give you a fair shot at me&quot;. You lose the ability to quietly deal with big problems, but you also diminish the chances of assassination and escalation.<br /> <br /> I would say using magic to manipulate others is considered rude and untrustworthy, a big reason Bearers of the Eternal Voice are seen with suspicion. But using it to enhance your skills is pretty normal, if you tell people before casting. A Moros is making his car into the MIB one as you talk , or has a ghost cook friend making everyone breakfast, the Mastigos keeps pulling stuff from his bag of holding, the Acanthus literally makes time to talk to the cabal in private, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T09:35:51-07:00","id":1332660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332064-how-magic-impacts-mage-society?p=1332637#post1332637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Targeting others is not a problem, depending on the method. Lets say you have an enemy who has sworn yoir death. If your cabal follows the Right of Nemesis, it means he can openly challenge you to a Duel Arcane. Can it be to the death ? Depends on the Consilium, but I would normally say not without a Hierarch's consent and some kind of mediation attempt by the Lex Magicka. The advantage of this custom is that it says to your enemies &quot;form a line and I will give you a fair shot at me&quot;. You lose the ability to quietly deal with big problems, but you also diminish the chances of assassination and escalation.<br /> <br /> I would say using magic to manipulate others is considered rude and untrustworthy, a big reason Bearers of the Eternal Voice are seen with suspicion. But using it to enhance your skills is pretty normal, if you tell people before casting. A Moros is making his car into the MIB one as you talk , or has a ghost cook friend making everyone breakfast, the Mastigos keeps pulling stuff from his bag of holding, the Acanthus literally makes time to talk to the cabal in private, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case obviously not^^<br /> What I meant was targeting someone with a spell is problematic if you want your relations with that someone to stay on non hostile terms <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> As for the second part, what I mentioned refers to magic used in social interactions between Mages, since I figured that's what OP asked.<br /> Enhancing your skills or attributes to ridiculous levels for example. If Bob had a persuasion skill of 1 and pumped it to a 4 or 5 every time he had to speak to other Mages at a gathering, people might get suspicious and start to laugh about Bob if, or rather when they find out,or feel tricked( \u201cBob used Magic to sweet talk me, I don't like that\u201d). Or if you used Fate Magic to make sure that your conversations went well, people might not look at that very favorable, etc.<br /> <br /> In the cases you mention, the Mage doesn't influence another Mage in an direct or indirect manner so mach as help out or show of. Things that of course are absolutely fine. (unleeees of course if the other Mage was a guardian. In that case, better don't overuse Magic^^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","user":"nobby","date":". 08-26-2019, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","name":"nobby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T13:15:36-07:00","id":1332709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nobby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332064-how-magic-impacts-mage-society?p=1332660#post1332660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that case obviously not^^<br /> What I meant was targeting someone with a spell is problematic if you want your relations with that someone to stay on non hostile terms <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> As for the second part, what I mentioned refers to magic used in social interactions between Mages, since I figured that's what OP asked.<br /> Enhancing your skills or attributes to ridiculous levels for example. If Bob had a persuasion skill of 1 and pumped it to a 4 or 5 every time he had to speak to other Mages at a gathering, people might get suspicious and start to laugh about Bob if, or rather when they find out,or feel tricked( \u201cBob used Magic to sweet talk me, I don't like that\u201d). Or if you used Fate Magic to make sure that your conversations went well, people might not look at that very favorable, etc.<br /> <br /> In the cases you mention, the Mage doesn't influence another Mage in an direct or indirect manner so mach as help out or show of. Things that of course are absolutely fine. (unleeees of course if the other Mage was a guardian. In that case, better don't overuse Magic^^)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, ok. In that case, I second Errol's recommendation and also add the Silver Ladder book, managing things is their specialty. They invented the Consilia, and the more I think analyze it, the more it sounds like a brilliant way to keep mages organized against their foes and away from each other's throats.<br /> <br /> In general I go by the rule that using any kind of magical manipulation is viewed by other mages as unacceptable, so you would need to be extremely careful to conceal it with Prime and even then discretion would be advised. Unless you are using it defensively to conceal your own research or sensitive Order/Consilium data. Makes the mage seem paranoid, but its reasonable. <br /> <br /> That just leaves favor trading via a prestation system, which is key to secure backing and resources. Regarding that topic I would like to recommend this article: <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2017/04/mage-awakening-2nd-ed-boon-system.html?m=1\" target=\"_blank\">https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2017/0...ystem.html?m=1</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-26-2019, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T12:05:47-07:00","id":1333143,"title":"","content":"Using magic to influence other mages is a bad thing to do for several reasons:<br /> <br /> 1. The Mage Sight is hard to deceive. With a Sleeper, you can quickly cast a spell on them without letting them know. It won't be that easy with a mage, because you'll immediately trip their Peripheral Sight and blast them with your Nimbus. Even if you cast something that makes you more likeable in your Sanctum, another mage can see the imago on you \u2013 and a Mastigos will definitely know what it does as soon as they take a peek with their Active Mage Sight.<br /> 2. You rarely deal with just one mage. Most likely they belong to a cabal, which means even more people who can detect your intrusion.<br /> 3. Most of them absolutely have means to retaliate.<br /> <br /> And I can't imagine such behavior being tolerated in any polite Consilium or Assembly. It's like drawing a weapon in a bar full of twitchy, armed gangers \u2013 maybe no one will escalate the situation, but if they do, it can spiral out of control very fast.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13425-gantolandon","name":"Gantolandon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T18:03:02-07:00","id":1333331,"title":"","content":"People dislike being manipulated, even by mundane means. And if you know the person who manipulated is a Mage and might have used to Magic, it must sting way worse. Even if they never cast on you specifically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T21:06:56-07:00","id":1333345,"title":"","content":"Grudges and petty arguments apparently linger. I've heard it compared to the academic field, with experienced mages holding ill will against newer wizards simply because they happened to be tutored by someone who disagreed with them (and perhaps got the consilium to agree with it) decades ago. I think it was in Sanctum and Sigil that really explored it but it's been a common thread throughout the books and blogs about the game (like <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/a-well-armed-society/\" target=\"_blank\">this one, 'A Well-Armed Society...'</a>). Perhaps it's a result of them being 'closer' to the Supernal, or perhaps it's just a natural result of them being the privileged of the world, but in general they don't seem to take being told they're (or heavens forbid, being proved) wrong very well. You wouldn't necessarily get a foaming mouthed rant and breakdown as you might in real life but there's a lot of little ways a mage can screw over another without rolling up on them in the consilium and slamming lightning bolts on them or charming everyone into a violent frenzy. Just getting in a position of 'authority' where you can say, 'I know you want to study this, but we've deemed it too dangerous,' or something can work. And that's the type of mundane thing you can get in real life, a mage could stymie your study into a rare type of geist by shutting down gates to the Underworld.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-31-2019, 12:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T06:41:35-07:00","id":1333381,"title":"","content":"Something I've long wondered what to do with is the presence of ghosts in the setting.<br /> <br /> Mummy introduced the idea to me that a cult could have members who had died and stuck around, which got me thinking about whether Mages would have a similar practice?<br /> <br /> Like, ghost mages are pretty powerful, and many would have wisdom that would be lost otherwise. In any case, by Diamond doctrine, they're not really the people they were, so who cares about them hanging around?<br /> <br /> I mean, you can easily come up with reasons that they might not do such a thing, but I thought it was interesting none the less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T11:12:04-07:00","id":1333410,"title":"","content":"What do you mean a similar practice? Like keeping ghost mages around for advice?<br /> <br /> It would probably be seen as a dangerous thing to do. Similar to spirits, ghosts are likely seen as tools, and having a ghost mage around would be like having a particularly dangerous tool laying around (some explosives, or a loaded weapon).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T12:03:10-07:00","id":1333417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332064-how-magic-impacts-mage-society?p=1333410#post1333410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean a similar practice? Like keeping ghost mages around for advice?</div> </div> </div> </div>More or less. Plus, they still have access to the arcana in a somewhat stunted manner (presuming that doesn't change in 2e). I mean, Mage already has the idea of using ghosts as fixed defensive systems and as familiars, this just takes it a bit farther. Also, both Mummy and Geist already have the practice so it's not unprecedented.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, 1e mentioned this as something that the Atlanteans had... the Cenotaph of Sighs I think it was.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It would probably be seen as a dangerous thing to do. Similar to spirits, ghosts are likely seen as tools, and having a ghost mage around would be like having a particularly dangerous tool laying around (some explosives, or a loaded weapon). </div> </div> </div>And to be honest, I think if I were seriously using this, I'd want it to be kinda dangerous. A way of giving literal weight to the history of the Diamond.<br /> <br /> This also goes for Spirits and Goetia. Like, S&amp;S does mention that the summoning of certain spirits to oversee consilia trials is not uncommon. So... what about Spirits of individual caucuses or Consilia?<br /> <br /> Also, one or two legacies had their own realms they used for <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">initiation, which is now more plausible as astral travel is much easier.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T12:04:47-07:00","id":1333419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332064-how-magic-impacts-mage-society?p=1333345#post1333345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grudges and petty arguments apparently linger. I've heard it compared to the academic field, with experienced mages holding ill will against newer wizards simply because they happened to be tutored by someone who disagreed with them (and perhaps got the consilium to agree with it) decades ago. I think it was in Sanctum and Sigil that really explored it but it's been a common thread throughout the books and blogs about the game (like <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/a-well-armed-society/&amp;quot;]this</a> one, 'A Well-Armed Society...'[/URL]). Perhaps it's a result of them being 'closer' to the Supernal, or perhaps it's just a natural result of them being the privileged of the world, but in general they don't seem to take being told they're (or heavens forbid, being proved) wrong very well. You wouldn't necessarily get a foaming mouthed rant and breakdown as you might in real life but there's a lot of little ways a mage can screw over another without rolling up on them in the consilium and slamming lightning bolts on them or charming everyone into a violent frenzy. Just getting in a position of 'authority' where you can say, 'I know you want to study this, but we've deemed it too dangerous,' or something can work. And that's the type of mundane thing you can get in real life, a mage could stymie your study into a rare type of geist by shutting down gates to the Underworld.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, which is why the Mysterium setup the guanxi system and its other protocols, to make it more likely for members to find their path unimpeded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T12:15:59-07:00","id":1333422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332064-how-magic-impacts-mage-society?p=1333381#post1333381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I've long wondered what to do with is the presence of ghosts in the setting.<br /> <br /> Mummy introduced the idea to me that a cult could have members who had died and stuck around, which got me thinking about whether Mages would have a similar practice?<br /> <br /> Like, ghost mages are pretty powerful, and many would have wisdom that would be lost otherwise. In any case, by Diamond doctrine, they're not really the people they were, so who cares about them hanging around?<br /> <br /> I mean, you can easily come up with reasons that they might not do such a thing, but I thought it was interesting none the less.</div> </div> </div> </div>A ghost mage would need someone or something he obsesses about strongly enough to want to remain after death.<br /> <br /> There is also fear. They know that after death the Psychopomp will probably go out of its way to bleach their soul, reset them to square zero and reincarmate them as Sleepers. Losing a lifetime of knowledge, being powerless again and being very vulnerable to Reapers, horrors of the Lower Depths, etc. That could scare a mage into making a backup ghost, or tethering their soul into a soul stone or locale. Of course, that also means lots of countermeasures and a certain desperation born from knowing they could die soon.<br /> <br /> So I would like to suggest using the stories of Exar Kun (for a Pentacle mage) and King Ommin (for a Seer). The ghost would want to trick his protege into reviving him. If his soul is banished to the Underworld, then he could feel desperate enough to give up his remaining Supernal might to become a Geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T08:44:18-07:00","id":1337328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332064-how-magic-impacts-mage-society?p=1333422#post1333422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A ghost mage would need someone or something he obsesses about strongly enough to want to remain after death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, you know, magic. Which admittedly would be vulnerable to dispelling","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T09:49:09-07:00","id":1337330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lareath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332064-how-magic-impacts-mage-society?p=1337328#post1337328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, you know, magic. Which admittedly would be vulnerable to dispelling</div> </div> </div> </div>If the spell is designed to ensure the creation of a ghost upon death, I would have it be Lasting as it's still the &quot;mundane&quot; act of dying that creates the ghost, unlike Create Ghost where it's the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T09:55:59-07:00","id":1337332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gantolandon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332064-how-magic-impacts-mage-society?p=1333143#post1333143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a Mastigos will definitely know what it does as soon as they take a peek with their Active Mage Sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>This requires a merit, scrutiny, or a spell. It's not going to be automatic from AMS alone. Whether or not going into someone's sanctum and actively scrutinizing the effects within is a faux pas or not is the sort of question I'm interested in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T10:20:38-07:00","id":1337336,"title":"","content":"Anyone who takes a look with Mind Sight will see that they're under a supernatural effect falling under the purview of Mind, but, as Inodiv says, nothing about what it does without deeper studies.<br /> Also, the Imago is only visible to AMS during the casting of the spell. Once the spell is cast (and pings PMS), the Imago is already gone. The Immediate Nimbus will be visible for a few turns at most, but that doesn't say anything about the spell's effect or even who's the subject of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T12:57:48-07:00","id":1337841,"title":"","content":"This reminds me of an Acanthus character I played who was brash and abrasive with anger management issues. She was often resentful and angry toward people for things they were <i>going</i> to do or things she'd witness them do in the past when she was not there. She also was highly distrustful of Mastigoi because she believed that they could make you <i>like</i> them... so as a personal rule, whenever she liked someone who happened to be a Warlock, she didn't trust her own feelings. Also, her skill with things of change and stuff is probably what made her so brash and reckless. Her virtue was Faith and she had complete faith in herself, her Fate and Time magic. She was always in the right place at the right time and everything happens for a reason.<br /> <br /> The effect on mage society is probably the reason mages have reputations for being eccentric, obsessive type of people. They're weird to outsiders, and can even be weird to other mages. You can have people like my character... but there are also people always notice, interact or even talk to things other people can't see, people who <i>know</i> they are speaking the truth and, as a result, believe they are always right, people who know whenever anyone lies or they know the instinct or motivation behind someone's words or actions, people who are always beautiful and healthy regardless of age, and other people who age prematurely due to the nature of their entropic magics or their weird relationship with time. Maybe someone is exceptionally materialistic and keeps all their personal belongings in pristine condition or someone who doesn't care anything for their personal belongings because they can just repair, modify, or manufacture anything they want. Maybe their attitudes extend to the people they interact with and stuff...<br /> <br /> I like to think about how each individual character's outlook shapes their interactions with others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}